From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yibo Wu <yibo.wu@perplexity.ai>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:14:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] alignment: carry the reference patch line onto upstream
 c5db9bd

Squashed port of reference_engines/vllm/patches 0001-0022 (based on
5629b26) onto c5db9bd. Upstream removed Model Runner V1 (#63373), so the
V1-only hunks are dropped and the V2 runner carries the alignment phases.
EngineCore iteration records now read scheduler_output.iteration_details;
EPLB record-only mode keeps upstream's create_model_communicator and
rearrangement status strings.

Patch 0020 (record DP dummy forwards in execute_dummy_batch) is carried
forward onto c5db9bd's own dummy path. c5db9bd adds an
EngineCoreProc.execute_dummy_batch override that publishes the GPU iteration
timings a dummy batch returns and does not call EngineCore's. It is the
method DPEngineCoreProc's busy loop reaches, so the log_dummy_forward wrapper
on EngineCore.execute_dummy_batch never ran there: idle DP ranks took no
forward ordinal and wrote no is_dummy record, and equal forward_ordinals on
two DP ranks stopped naming the same global step. The override now wraps the
executor call in log_dummy_forward too. tests/v1/engine/test_iteration_logging.py
covers the busy loop's path: one ordinal and one record per dummy forward,
the GPU timings still published, and nothing recorded with logging off.
